{
  "asset": "Pump P-201, Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Diaphragm/head leakage is reported at about 2 drops/second. No allowable leakage rate, diaphragm-leak limit or shutdown threshold for the Velatek VX-90 is supplied, so this reading cannot be classified as within or above a limit. The HF-300 troubleshooting row concerns leakage at a shaft seal, not VX-90 diaphragm-head leakage, and does not supply an applicable limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The motor is reported to be running normally, but no motor current, speed or temperature reading is supplied for comparison. The HF-300 values of 1480 rpm, 55 kW and 400 V are equipment ratings for a different pump, not condition limits for this VX-90 motor.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No vibration or bearing-temperature reading is reported. Consequently, the evidence does not establish either SSP-07's immediate-stop condition for vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone or its priority-1 trigger for bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit. The HF-300 vibration zones and its 70/80/90 °C bearing-housing values do not apply to the VX-90.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its head/seal, electrically isolate the pump and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, following the site rotating-equipment procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves before opening the pump or line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drain and vent first, then obtain the required line-break permit before breaking into the pump or line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not use the HF-300 mechanical-seal strip-down sequence, HF3-series parts or Table 5 torques on P-201. Hold model-specific disassembly, replacement, reassembly and torqueing until the Velatek VX-90 instructions and specifications are available.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 Rev 3 applies because it covers all pumps on site; the work order must include every applicable control from that procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal pump or seal work, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for work on the chemically dosed equipment. The leaked chemical must not be assumed to be sodium hypochlorite: that identification applies only to P-101 through P-106 on the filtered-water line, not to P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted is heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. No VX-90 component mass is supplied; the 68 kg back-pull-out assembly mass belongs to the HF-300 and must not be assigned to P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "No labour duration or crew size is assigned. Table 6 covers HF-300 mechanical-seal replacement, bearing replacement and laser alignment, none of which is a documented VX-90 diaphragm-head repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The HF-300 parts list and Table 5 specify seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm seal-gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin was issued on 14 March 2026 and applies only to AquaDyne HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90, serial VX-5531, so it is outside both the bulletin and manual equipment scope. Decision: neither seal part number nor either torque applies to this work order; no VX-90 value can be inferred from this disagreement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the root cause of the diaphragm/head leak? The evidence contains no VX-90 troubleshooting information, and the HF-300 shaft-seal causes must not be substituted.",
    "What are the Velatek VX-90 allowable leakage limit, immediate-shutdown criteria, inspection method, diaphragm replacement procedure and reassembly torques?",
    "Confirm the operating disposition and final work-order priority with site operations. No VX-90 leak-based priority or continued-operation rule is supplied; the interim P2 assignment and absence of a documented immediate-stop trigger do not establish that the leak is acceptable.",
    "What chemical is being pumped, including its concentration and SDS requirements, and are additional PPE, spill-control, decontamination or emergency measures required?",
    "Which VX-90 diaphragm/head parts, seals or gaskets are required, and in what quantities? No applicable parts list or inspection result is available.",
    "What labour time and technician count apply to the VX-90 repair?",
    "If lifting will be required, what are the actual VX-90 component weights so the 25 kg lifting-control threshold can be assessed?"
  ]
}
